      "securityImpact": "A producer that can influence captured test log bytes, or malformed control output from a test/fixture, can amplify CI verifier CPU and delay evidence rejection. The unchanged Vitest gate parses the entire text twice (file and test counts); the 131115-byte sample took 4094 ms before failing closed. This is CI availability, not a reproduced remote API exploit or approval bypass.",
      "dataflow": [
        "phase10-verify.mjs:73-82 reads the supplied artifact into a Buffer without an input-size check in that reader",
        "certification-rules.mjs:1299-1336 reads and hashes raw log, checks header binding, and passes log to deriveGateOutcome",
        "certification-rules.mjs:616-637 converts the entire log to UTF-8 and invokes parseVitestSummary twice",
        "certification-rules.mjs:559-563 performs the unanchored OSC replacement before the null guard"
      ],
      "exploitPreconditions": "Control over captured test-output bytes; the probe is entirely synthetic. No network-facing reachability is asserted. Runtime-specific sample timings may vary.",
      "remediation": "Use a bounded linear state-machine scan for OSC terminators and fail closed on unfinished sequences, or an equivalent proven linear normalizer. Validate repeated unterminated ESC and C1 cases while retaining first-failure/count semantics. No patch made.",
